{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792528579145,"sessionID":"ses_ea4f89b40ffeJA5Vf8sjCWqpcq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_pm2YG5aVJQCOC93j8yuE1755","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\20-brief.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\20-brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief — 2026-10-20\n2: \n3: ## The use case\n4: \n5: Geocachers hitting a find-count milestone want one clean, deterministic \"I hit\n6: 1,000 finds\" share card, built from the numbers their own My Finds pocket-query\n7: GPX already contains (find count, cache-type mix, FTFs, difficulty/terrain),\n8: instead of a hand-built profile banner. The moment repeats at every milestone\n9: and every year-in-review, and it is served today by Project-GC's Milestones tab\n10: and hand-made banners, not by a reproducible per-milestone render.\n11: \n12: ## The template\n13: \n14: - id: `@one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1` — pack `community`, no new\n15:   pack: geocaching is a hobby community that makes cards for its own members from\n16:   the record it already keeps (the My Finds GPX), which is exactly the pack's\n17:   description.\n18: - title: `Geocache Milestone Card` (the scaffold prefixes `2026-10-20 · `, tags\n19:   `day-031`).\n20: - kind: image (still PNG); canvas hint `1080x1080`; must also render cleanly at\n21:   landscape (`1920x1080`) and portrait (`1080x1920`) — and pass the build's\n22:   7-canvas layout sweep (1920x1080 · 1280x720 · 1080x1920 · 1080x1080 · 3840x2160\n23:   · 640x360 · 480x270).\n24: - duration: still (no clock; `outputHints.format { kind: \"image\", container: \"png\" }`).\n25: \n26: ## Layout (regions, ratios — no pixels)\n27: \n28: Square/portrait stack four bands; landscape puts the header and the hero side by\n29: side and the mix and the tiles below.\n30: \n31: ```\n32: +------------------------------------------+\n33: | GEOCACHING              NAME (caps)      |  header ~16% : name, \"GEOCACHING\",\n34: | caching since YYYY      [accent rule]    |  \"caching since YYYY\", accent rule\n35: +------------------------------------------+\n36: |                                          |\n37: |   1,000                                   |  hero ~42% : the find count,\n38: |   1,000th find  [ MILESTONE ]             |  the derived ordinal line,\n39: |                                          |  badge only when it IS a milestone\n40: +------------------------------------------+\n41: | ##### ==== ## ##                          |  mix ~20% : full-width stacked bar\n42: | Trad 812 · Mystery 121 · Multi 38 ...     |  (top types, \"Other\" = remainder),\n43: |                                          |  one legend line under it\n44: +------------------------------------------+\n45: |   FTF    |  Avg D   |  Avg T              |  tiles ~16% : three equal stat tiles\n46: |    24    |   2.3    |   1.8               |\n47: +------------------------------------------+\n48: |  footer line (optional, \"\" drops it)      |  footer ~6%\n49: +------------------------------------------+\n50: ```\n51: \n52: The one design decision: **the milestone is computed, never typed.** The big\n53: number is the find count; the card derives the ordinal (\"1,000th\", \"1,042nd\") and\n54: whether that count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the `MILESTONE` badge\n55: only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about, so the\n56: card cannot disagree with itself.\n57: \n58: ## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps at 7 canvases)\n59: \n60: - Every text fits its box — `textFitsMeasured` on each text source; `svgLabel`\n61:   legend copy under `textFitsAll`.\n62: - Header in the top band: `name` within `yFrac [0, 0.24]`.\n63: - The hero count is present and is the largest text on the card; the derived\n64:   ordinal line sits directly under it (`find-count` and `milestone-line` present,\n65:   `milestone-line` within `yFrac [0.15, 0.6]`).\n66: - The mix bar is full-width: `type-mix-bar` `minWidthFrac: 0.9`, within `yFrac\n67:   [0.3, 0.78]`.\n68: - The three stat tiles are one size: `equal: \"size\"` over `tile-ftf`, `tile-d`,\n69:   `tile-t` (tolerance 2px).\n70: - Footer band: `footer` within `yFrac [0.86, 1]` when present; when `\"\"` the\n71:   space returns to the card (band never reserved empty).\n72: - A square `MILESTONE` badge `aspect: 1` when present (findCount is a milestone).\n73: \n74: ## Props (8 + debugLayout)\n75: \n76: | name | type | default | what it changes | required |\n77: |---|---|---|---|---|\n78: | `cacherName` | string | `\"geohiker55\"` | header name, drawn in capitals | no |\n79: | `findCount` | number | `1000` | hero number; drives the derived ordinal + badge | no |\n80: | `ftfCount` | number | `24` | first-to-find stat tile | no |\n81: | `avgD` | number | `2.3` | average difficulty tile (1.0–5.0, one decimal) | no |\n82: | `avgT` | number | `1.8` | average terrain tile (1.0–5.0, one decimal) | no |\n83: | `sinceYear` | number | `2015` | \"caching since YYYY\" header subline (2000–2026) | no |\n84: | `typeMix` | json | 5 entries | the mix bar + legend; top 5 by count, remainder = \"Other\" | no |\n85: | `accent` | string color | `#4a8f3c` | hero number, badge fill, header rule | no |\n86: | `debugLayout` | boolean | `false` | draws the layout contract over the card | no |\n87: \n88: `typeMix` is a list of `{ \"type\": \"<name>\", \"count\": <int> }`. Recognized types\n89: and their fixed palette (bar segments use this, not `accent`): Traditional,\n90: Multi, Mystery, Letterbox, Earthcache, Virtual, Webcam, Event, CITO, Wherigo,\n91: Adventure Lab. A type name outside this set is refused by name (with a\n92: \"did you mean\" hint); counts are integers >= 0; only the top 5 by count render,\n93: and the bar's remainder (`findCount - sum of the shown`) draws as a gray\n94: `Other` segment so the bar always spans the full width.\n95: \n96: Derived helper (pure, exported, unit-tested): `isMilestone(n)` follows\n97: Project-GC — 1, 10, 50, 100; then `n % 100 == 0` for 100 < n <= 1000; then\n98: `n % 500 == 0` for 1000 < n <= 5000; then `n % 1000 == 0` for n > 5000.\n99: `ordinal(n)` formats with thousands separators and the right suffix\n100: (\"1,000th\", \"1,042nd\", \"11th\", \"21st\").\n101: \n102: ## Beats\n103: \n104: Still — no beats.\n105: \n106: ## Defaults must show\n107: \n108: A viewer with no inputs sees an invented geocacher (`geohiker55`) at **1,000\n109: finds**: the big \"1,000\", the derived \"1,000th find\" line and the `MILESTONE`\n110: badge (1000 is a milestone), a full-width five-type mix bar with no `Other`\n111: segment (the default counts sum exactly to 1000), and the three tiles (24 FTF,\n112: 2.3 avg D, 1.8 avg T), on the light paper with the green accent. The sample is\n113: labelled invented in the schema copy, like the neighbours.\n114: \n115: ## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n116: \n117: 1. At defaults the card renders complete — name, hero count, ordinal + badge,\n118:    mix bar + legend, three tiles — with no clipped or overlapping text at any of\n119:    the seven contract canvases.\n120: 2. The milestone is correct: `findCount` 1000 -> \"1,000th\" + badge; 1042 ->\n121:    \"1,042nd\", no badge; the ordinal suffix and `isMilestone` ladder match\n122:    Project-GC exactly (1, 10, 50, 100, 200...1000, 1500...5000, 6000...).\n123: 3. The mix is honest: top 5 types by count, unknown type refused by name,\n124:    remainder drawn as gray \"Other\" so the bar always spans full width; the legend\n125:    copy fits its cell at every canvas.\n126: 4. Deterministic and fail-fast: identical props give an identical document; no\n127:    clock, no `Math.random`; a bad value (non-integer findCount, avgD outside\n128:    1–5, a misspelled type) throws an error naming the field.\n129: 5. The layout contract holds (text fits, header top band, full-width mix bar,\n130:    three equal tiles, footer band), and all default copy is printable ASCII.\n131: \n132: ## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea different)\n133: \n134: - **a — hero posture:** the baseline left-aligns the hero count under the header;\n135:   variant a centres the count and blows it up, collapsing the header to just the\n136:   name line. Same data, different hierarchy.\n137: - **b — mix as rows:** replace the horizontal stacked bar with a vertical list of\n138:   per-type rows (name + proportional count bar), which gives long type names room\n139:   on portrait. Same data, different mix rendering.\n140: - **c — night-cache preset:** add a `preset` \"dark\" | \"light\" with a navy page\n141:   and retuned contrast (the \"night cache\"), versus the light paper baseline.\n142:   Same layout, different palette.\n\n(End of file - total 142 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief — 2026-10-20\n\n## The use case\n\nGeocachers hitting a find-count milestone want one clean, deterministic \"I hit\n1,000 finds\" share card, built from the numbers their own My Finds pocket-query\nGPX already contains (find count, cache-type mix, FTFs, difficulty/terrain),\ninstead of a hand-built profile banner. The moment repeats at every milestone\nand every year-in-review, and it is served today by Project-GC's Milestones tab\nand hand-made banners, not by a reproducible per-milestone render.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1` — pack `community`, no new\n  pack: geocaching is a hobby community that makes cards for its own members from\n  the record it already keeps (the My Finds GPX), which is exactly the pack's\n  description.\n- title: `Geocache Milestone Card` (the scaffold prefixes `2026-10-20 · `, tags\n  `day-031`).\n- kind: image (still PNG); canvas hint `1080x1080`; must also render cleanly at","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\20-brief.md","text":"# Brief — 2026-10-20\n\n## The use case\n\nGeocachers hitting a find-count milestone want one clean, deterministic \"I hit\n1,000 finds\" share card, built from the numbers their own My Finds pocket-query\nGPX already contains (find count, cache-type mix, FTFs, difficulty/terrain),\ninstead of a hand-built profile banner. The moment repeats at every milestone\nand every year-in-review, and it is served today by Project-GC's Milestones tab\nand hand-made banners, not by a reproducible per-milestone render.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1` — pack `community`, no new\n  pack: geocaching is a hobby community that makes cards for its own members from\n  the record it already keeps (the My Finds GPX), which is exactly the pack's\n  description.\n- title: `Geocache Milestone Card` (the scaffold prefixes `2026-10-20 · `, tags\n  `day-031`).\n- kind: image (still PNG); canvas hint `1080x1080`; must also render cleanly at\n  landscape (`1920x1080`) and portrait (`1080x1920`) — and pass the build's\n  7-canvas layout sweep (1920x1080 · 1280x720 · 1080x1920 · 1080x1080 · 3840x2160\n  · 640x360 · 480x270).\n- duration: still (no clock; `outputHints.format { kind: \"image\", container: \"png\" }`).\n\n## Layout (regions, ratios — no pixels)\n\nSquare/portrait stack four bands; landscape puts the header and the hero side by\nside and the mix and the tiles below.\n\n```\n+------------------------------------------+\n| GEOCACHING              NAME (caps)      |  header ~16% : name, \"GEOCACHING\",\n| caching since YYYY      [accent rule]    |  \"caching since YYYY\", accent rule\n+------------------------------------------+\n|                                          |\n|   1,000                                   |  hero ~42% : the find count,\n|   1,000th find  [ MILESTONE ]             |  the derived ordinal line,\n|                                          |  badge only when it IS a milestone\n+------------------------------------------+\n| ##### ==== ## ##                          |  mix ~20% : full-width stacked bar\n| Trad 812 · Mystery 121 · Multi 38 ...     |  (top types, \"Other\" = remainder),\n|                                          |  one legend line under it\n+------------------------------------------+\n|   FTF    |  Avg D   |  Avg T              |  tiles ~16% : three equal stat tiles\n|    24    |   2.3    |   1.8               |\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  footer line (optional, \"\" drops it)      |  footer ~6%\n+------------------------------------------+\n```\n\nThe one design decision: **the milestone is computed, never typed.** The big\nnumber is the find count; the card derives the ordinal (\"1,000th\", \"1,042nd\") and\nwhether that count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the `MILESTONE` badge\nonly when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about, so the\ncard cannot disagree with itself.\n\n## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps at 7 canvases)\n\n- Every text fits its box — `textFitsMeasured` on each text source; `svgLabel`\n  legend copy under `textFitsAll`.\n- Header in the top band: `name` within `yFrac [0, 0.24]`.\n- The hero count is present and is the largest text on the card; the derived\n  ordinal line sits directly under it (`find-count` and `milestone-line` present,\n  `milestone-line` within `yFrac [0.15, 0.6]`).\n- The mix bar is full-width: `type-mix-bar` `minWidthFrac: 0.9`, within `yFrac\n  [0.3, 0.78]`.\n- The three stat tiles are one size: `equal: \"size\"` over `tile-ftf`, `tile-d`,\n  `tile-t` (tolerance 2px).\n- Footer band: `footer` within `yFrac [0.86, 1]` when present; when `\"\"` the\n  space returns to the card (band never reserved empty).\n- A square `MILESTONE` badge `aspect: 1` when present (findCount is a milestone).\n\n## Props (8 + debugLayout)\n\n| name | type | default | what it changes | required |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `cacherName` | string | `\"geohiker55\"` | header name, drawn in capitals | no |\n| `findCount` | number | `1000` | hero number; drives the derived ordinal + badge | no |\n| `ftfCount` | number | `24` | first-to-find stat tile | no |\n| `avgD` | number | `2.3` | average difficulty tile (1.0–5.0, one decimal) | no |\n| `avgT` | number | `1.8` | average terrain tile (1.0–5.0, one decimal) | no |\n| `sinceYear` | number | `2015` | \"caching since YYYY\" header subline (2000–2026) | no |\n| `typeMix` | json | 5 entries | the mix bar + legend; top 5 by count, remainder = \"Other\" | no |\n| `accent` | string color | `#4a8f3c` | hero number, badge fill, header rule | no |\n| `debugLayout` | boolean | `false` | draws the layout contract over the card | no |\n\n`typeMix` is a list of `{ \"type\": \"<name>\", \"count\": <int> }`. Recognized types\nand their fixed palette (bar segments use this, not `accent`): Traditional,\nMulti, Mystery, Letterbox, Earthcache, Virtual, Webcam, Event, CITO, Wherigo,\nAdventure Lab. A type name outside this set is refused by name (with a\n\"did you mean\" hint); counts are integers >= 0; only the top 5 by count render,\nand the bar's remainder (`findCount - sum of the shown`) draws as a gray\n`Other` segment so the bar always spans the full width.\n\nDerived helper (pure, exported, unit-tested): `isMilestone(n)` follows\nProject-GC — 1, 10, 50, 100; then `n % 100 == 0` for 100 < n <= 1000; then\n`n % 500 == 0` for 1000 < n <= 5000; then `n % 1000 == 0` for n > 5000.\n`ordinal(n)` formats with thousands separators and the right suffix\n(\"1,000th\", \"1,042nd\", \"11th\", \"21st\").\n\n## Beats\n\nStill — no beats.\n\n## Defaults must show\n\nA viewer with no inputs sees an invented geocacher (`geohiker55`) at **1,000\nfinds**: the big \"1,000\", the derived \"1,000th find\" line and the `MILESTONE`\nbadge (1000 is a milestone), a full-width five-type mix bar with no `Other`\nsegment (the default counts sum exactly to 1000), and the three tiles (24 FTF,\n2.3 avg D, 1.8 avg T), on the light paper with the green accent. The sample is\nlabelled invented in the schema copy, like the neighbours.\n\n## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n\n1. At defaults the card renders complete — name, hero count, ordinal + badge,\n   mix bar + legend, three tiles — with no clipped or overlapping text at any of\n   the seven contract canvases.\n2. The milestone is correct: `findCount` 1000 -> \"1,000th\" + badge; 1042 ->\n   \"1,042nd\", no badge; the ordinal suffix and `isMilestone` ladder match\n   Project-GC exactly (1, 10, 50, 100, 200...1000, 1500...5000, 6000...).\n3. The mix is honest: top 5 types by count, unknown type refused by name,\n   remainder drawn as gray \"Other\" so the bar always spans full width; the legend\n   copy fits its cell at every canvas.\n4. Deterministic and fail-fast: identical props give an identical document; no\n   clock, no `Math.random`; a bad value (non-integer findCount, avgD outside\n   1–5, a misspelled type) throws an error naming the field.\n5. The layout contract holds (text fits, header top band, full-width mix bar,\n   three equal tiles, footer band), and all default copy is printable ASCII.\n\n## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea different)\n\n- **a — hero posture:** the baseline left-aligns the hero count under the header;\n  variant a centres the count and blows it up, collapsing the header to just the\n  name line. Same data, different hierarchy.\n- **b — mix as rows:** replace the horizontal stacked bar with a vertical list of\n  per-type rows (name + proportional count bar), which gives long type names room\n  on portrait. Same data, different mix rendering.\n- **c — night-cache preset:** add a `preset` \"dark\" | \"light\" with a navy page\n  and retuned contrast (the \"night cache\"), versus the light paper baseline.\n  Same layout, different palette.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":142,"totalLines":142,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-20\\20-brief.md","time":{"start":1792528579126,"end":1792528579142}},"id":"prt_15b0779cb001TgdwJ87tP2G27P","sessionID":"ses_ea4f89b40ffeJA5Vf8sjCWqpcq","messageID":"msg_15b0767350010wHqvIDshhxF9C"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792528579351,"sessionID":"ses_ea4f89b40ffeJA5Vf8sjCWqpcq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_sK2lOEHrF3C3A22k9sT69015","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\10-scout.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\10-scout.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Scout — 2026-10-20\n2: \n3: ## Candidates (4, best first)\n4: \n5: ### 1. Geocaching milestone / profile-stat card\n6: - Who: Geocachers who hit a milestone or want a stats card, gathered on the\n7:   Geocaching forums (forums.geocaching.com), the Project-GC stats site, and\n8:   their local clubs (e.g. YoGO posts a \"congratulations on 1000 finds\" note for\n9:   every member who reaches one).\n10: - The construct: the find count and its milestones. The first milestones are 1,\n11:   10, 50 and 100 finds, then every hundred to 1000, every five hundred to 5000,\n12:   then every thousand (Project-GC \"Milestones tab\"). The artifact every Premium\n13:   member already has is the **My Finds pocket query** — a zipped GPX of every\n14:   cache they logged, with per-find log date/type, cache type, and\n15:   difficulty/terrain.\n16: - The recurring need: a shareable \"I hit N finds\" card or profile-stats banner,\n17:   generated from the GPX they already download. CacheSleuth already reads the\n18:   My Finds GPX and builds a profile *banner* from it (Overview / Charts / Grids\n19:   / Milestones / FTF / Finds sections), which the cacher pastes into their\n20:   profile. Project-GC has a whole Milestones tab and BadgeGen badges. The\n21:   moment repeats on every milestone and every \"year in review\".\n22: - Evidence:\n23:   - https://www.cachesleuth.com/tools/profilestats — \"Upload your My Finds pocket\n24:     query and see your geocaching statistics... [publish] a profile banner\"\n25:     built from Overview / Charts / Grids / Milestones / FTF / Finds.\n26:   - https://project-gc.com/w/Milestones_tab — \"The first milestones are 1, 10, 50\n27:     and 100 caches, after that and up to 1000 caches every hundredth cache is\n28:     considered a milestone.\"\n29:   - https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2025/05/celebrating-25-years-of-geocaching-milestones\n30:     — \"As geocachers, we love milestones! We remember our first find, our first\n31:     hide, the first Event we attended, our first international find...\"\n32:   - https://www.geocaching.com/help/index.php?id=118&pg=kb.page — the \"My Finds\"\n33:     pocket query \"returns all geocaches you found, including archived geocaches,\n34:     and your log entries\", a zipped GPX.\n35:   - https://www.yogosc.org/announcements/congratulations-to-geohiker55-on-1000-finds\n36:     — a local club announces \"geohiker55 found his 1000th find yesterday\".\n37: - Why m0saic fits: rectangles on a canvas. A card with a big find-count, the\n38:   milestone ordinal (\"1,000th\"), a cache-type breakdown as a small bar/pip row,\n39:   FTF count, and a difficulty/terrain cell; props mirror the GPX fields\n40:   (findCount, milestone, types per cache type, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, year). Batch\n41:   one card per milestone or per year; deterministic, no GUI.\n42: - Risks: the GPX itself must be parsed outside the template (props are the\n43:   already-derived numbers), cache types are numerous (cap the mix to the top few),\n44:   and existing tools (Project-GC, CacheSleuth) already show stats — so the angle\n45:   must be the clean, deterministic *share card*, not another stats dashboard.\n46: \n47: ### 2. Disc golf round recap card (UDisc)\n48: - Who: Disc golfers on r/discgolf and UDisc leagues; UDisc logs rounds with\n49:   hole-by-hole scores, birdies/pars/bogeys, and a UDisc/PDGA rating.\n50: - The construct: a round, scored against par, with a rating. Artifact: UDisc\n51:   round data and its league \"Export\" (CSV).\n52: - The recurring need: a clean per-round recap card (score, rating, birdies,\n53:   bogeys, ace) to share after a good round or an ace.\n54: - Evidence: https://udisc.com/events/... leaderboards with per-hole scores and\n55:   \"Rating | Round\"; http://jim.roepcke.com/blog/archives/2025/01/01/year-in-review-2024.html\n56:   — \"According to UDisc I played 108 rounds... 286 birdies, 946 pars, 270 bogeys\".\n57: - Why m0saic fits: batchable round cards, props mirror the scorecard.\n58: - Risks: nearly the same shape as the day-21 golf scorecard (birdie/bogey grid),\n59:   and UDisc already has strong native share surfaces.\n60: \n61: ### 3. FPV drone flight recap (Betaflight blackbox)\n62: - Who: FPV pilots on intoFPV.com, RCGroups, and the Betaflight Discord; the\n63:   flight controller writes a `.bbl` blackbox log per armed flight.\n64: - The construct: a flight, with telemetry (top speed, altitude, flight time,\n65:   battery, RSSI). Artifact: `.bbl` logs decodable to CSV via `blackbox_decode`.\n66: - The recurring need: a flight recap card/clip to share after a good session.\n67: - Evidence: https://ghosttracefpv.com — \"FLIGHT RECAP — Written from your\n68:   telemetry once the flight is on your account\"; https://betaflight.com/docs/wiki/guides/current/Black-Box-logging-and-usage.\n69: - Why m0saic fits: deterministic recap from decoded CSV fields.\n70: - Risks: community behavior skews toward PID tuning, not sharing recaps, and\n71:   GhostTrace already generates the recap card.\n72: \n73: ### 4. Bowling league series / milestone card (USBC)\n74: - Who: USBC league bowlers; the construct is the series and the 300 game / 700 /\n75:   800 series milestones.\n76: - Artifact: USBC \"Bowler Average Sheet\" and league standing sheets, not a clean\n77:   per-bowler file a player exports themselves.\n78: - The recurring need: a \"I rolled a 300\" or season-average card.\n79: - Evidence: https://membership.bowl.com/USBCsearch/ViewMember-LeagueSheet.jsp,\n80:   https://bowl.com/a-future-for-the-sport/2026-state-of-the-association.\n81: - Why m0saic fits: a clean scorecard/award card.\n82: - Risks: artifact lives with the league secretary, not the bowler; USBC already\n83:   issues awards, so the \"make it yourself\" need is thinner.\n84: \n85: ## Pick\n86: \n87: **Geocaching milestone / profile-stat card.** It is the most on-thesis niche of\n88: the day: a community organised around one construct (the find count and its\n89: milestones) with a shared artifact every member already downloads (the My Finds\n90: GPX), and a recurring show-off moment (milestones and year-in-review) still\n91: served today by hand-built banners. It is also cleanly distinct from all 30\n92: prior days — no geocaching template exists.\n93: \n94: ## Rejected today\n95: - Disc golf round recap: too close to the day-21 golf scorecard and UDisc already shares natively.\n96: - FPV drone flight recap: tuning-focused community, and GhostTrace already ships the recap card.\n97: - Bowling league series card: the artifact sits with the league secretary, and USBC awards cover it.\n\n(End of file - total 97 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Scout — 2026-10-20\n\n## Candidates (4, best first)\n\n### 1. Geocaching milestone / profile-stat card\n- Who: Geocachers who hit a milestone or want a stats card, gathered on the\n  Geocaching forums (forums.geocaching.com), the Project-GC stats site, and\n  their local clubs (e.g. YoGO posts a \"congratulations on 1000 finds\" note for\n  every member who reaches one).\n- The construct: the find count and its milestones. The first milestones are 1,\n  10, 50 and 100 finds, then every hundred to 1000, every five hundred to 5000,\n  then every thousand (Project-GC \"Milestones tab\"). The artifact every Premium\n  member already has is the **My Finds pocket query** — a zipped GPX of every\n  cache they logged, with per-find log date/type, cache type, and\n  difficulty/terrain.\n- The recurring need: a shareable \"I hit N finds\" card or profile-stats banner,\n  generated from the GPX they already download. CacheSleuth already reads the\n  My Finds GPX and builds a profile *banner* from it (Overview / Charts / Grids\n  / Milestones / FTF / Finds sections), which the cacher pastes into their\n  profile. Project-GC has a whole Milestones tab and BadgeGen badges. The","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\10-scout.md","text":"# Scout — 2026-10-20\n\n## Candidates (4, best first)\n\n### 1. Geocaching milestone / profile-stat card\n- Who: Geocachers who hit a milestone or want a stats card, gathered on the\n  Geocaching forums (forums.geocaching.com), the Project-GC stats site, and\n  their local clubs (e.g. YoGO posts a \"congratulations on 1000 finds\" note for\n  every member who reaches one).\n- The construct: the find count and its milestones. The first milestones are 1,\n  10, 50 and 100 finds, then every hundred to 1000, every five hundred to 5000,\n  then every thousand (Project-GC \"Milestones tab\"). The artifact every Premium\n  member already has is the **My Finds pocket query** — a zipped GPX of every\n  cache they logged, with per-find log date/type, cache type, and\n  difficulty/terrain.\n- The recurring need: a shareable \"I hit N finds\" card or profile-stats banner,\n  generated from the GPX they already download. CacheSleuth already reads the\n  My Finds GPX and builds a profile *banner* from it (Overview / Charts / Grids\n  / Milestones / FTF / Finds sections), which the cacher pastes into their\n  profile. Project-GC has a whole Milestones tab and BadgeGen badges. The\n  moment repeats on every milestone and every \"year in review\".\n- Evidence:\n  - https://www.cachesleuth.com/tools/profilestats — \"Upload your My Finds pocket\n    query and see your geocaching statistics... [publish] a profile banner\"\n    built from Overview / Charts / Grids / Milestones / FTF / Finds.\n  - https://project-gc.com/w/Milestones_tab — \"The first milestones are 1, 10, 50\n    and 100 caches, after that and up to 1000 caches every hundredth cache is\n    considered a milestone.\"\n  - https://www.geocaching.com/blog/2025/05/celebrating-25-years-of-geocaching-milestones\n    — \"As geocachers, we love milestones! We remember our first find, our first\n    hide, the first Event we attended, our first international find...\"\n  - https://www.geocaching.com/help/index.php?id=118&pg=kb.page — the \"My Finds\"\n    pocket query \"returns all geocaches you found, including archived geocaches,\n    and your log entries\", a zipped GPX.\n  - https://www.yogosc.org/announcements/congratulations-to-geohiker55-on-1000-finds\n    — a local club announces \"geohiker55 found his 1000th find yesterday\".\n- Why m0saic fits: rectangles on a canvas. A card with a big find-count, the\n  milestone ordinal (\"1,000th\"), a cache-type breakdown as a small bar/pip row,\n  FTF count, and a difficulty/terrain cell; props mirror the GPX fields\n  (findCount, milestone, types per cache type, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, year). Batch\n  one card per milestone or per year; deterministic, no GUI.\n- Risks: the GPX itself must be parsed outside the template (props are the\n  already-derived numbers), cache types are numerous (cap the mix to the top few),\n  and existing tools (Project-GC, CacheSleuth) already show stats — so the angle\n  must be the clean, deterministic *share card*, not another stats dashboard.\n\n### 2. Disc golf round recap card (UDisc)\n- Who: Disc golfers on r/discgolf and UDisc leagues; UDisc logs rounds with\n  hole-by-hole scores, birdies/pars/bogeys, and a UDisc/PDGA rating.\n- The construct: a round, scored against par, with a rating. Artifact: UDisc\n  round data and its league \"Export\" (CSV).\n- The recurring need: a clean per-round recap card (score, rating, birdies,\n  bogeys, ace) to share after a good round or an ace.\n- Evidence: https://udisc.com/events/... leaderboards with per-hole scores and\n  \"Rating | Round\"; http://jim.roepcke.com/blog/archives/2025/01/01/year-in-review-2024.html\n  — \"According to UDisc I played 108 rounds... 286 birdies, 946 pars, 270 bogeys\".\n- Why m0saic fits: batchable round cards, props mirror the scorecard.\n- Risks: nearly the same shape as the day-21 golf scorecard (birdie/bogey grid),\n  and UDisc already has strong native share surfaces.\n\n### 3. FPV drone flight recap (Betaflight blackbox)\n- Who: FPV pilots on intoFPV.com, RCGroups, and the Betaflight Discord; the\n  flight controller writes a `.bbl` blackbox log per armed flight.\n- The construct: a flight, with telemetry (top speed, altitude, flight time,\n  battery, RSSI). Artifact: `.bbl` logs decodable to CSV via `blackbox_decode`.\n- The recurring need: a flight recap card/clip to share after a good session.\n- Evidence: https://ghosttracefpv.com — \"FLIGHT RECAP — Written from your\n  telemetry once the flight is on your account\"; https://betaflight.com/docs/wiki/guides/current/Black-Box-logging-and-usage.\n- Why m0saic fits: deterministic recap from decoded CSV fields.\n- Risks: community behavior skews toward PID tuning, not sharing recaps, and\n  GhostTrace already generates the recap card.\n\n### 4. Bowling league series / milestone card (USBC)\n- Who: USBC league bowlers; the construct is the series and the 300 game / 700 /\n  800 series milestones.\n- Artifact: USBC \"Bowler Average Sheet\" and league standing sheets, not a clean\n  per-bowler file a player exports themselves.\n- The recurring need: a \"I rolled a 300\" or season-average card.\n- Evidence: https://membership.bowl.com/USBCsearch/ViewMember-LeagueSheet.jsp,\n  https://bowl.com/a-future-for-the-sport/2026-state-of-the-association.\n- Why m0saic fits: a clean scorecard/award card.\n- Risks: artifact lives with the league secretary, not the bowler; USBC already\n  issues awards, so the \"make it yourself\" need is thinner.\n\n## Pick\n\n**Geocaching milestone / profile-stat card.** It is the most on-thesis niche of\nthe day: a community organised around one construct (the find count and its\nmilestones) with a shared artifact every member already downloads (the My Finds\nGPX), and a recurring show-off moment (milestones and year-in-review) still\nserved today by hand-built banners. It is also cleanly distinct from all 30\nprior days — no geocaching template exists.\n\n## Rejected today\n- Disc golf round recap: too close to the day-21 golf scorecard and UDisc already shares natively.\n- FPV drone flight recap: tuning-focused community, and GhostTrace already ships the recap card.\n- Bowling league series card: the artifact sits with the league secretary, and USBC awards cover it.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":97,"totalLines":97,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-20\\10-scout.md","time":{"start":1792528579336,"end":1792528579349}},"id":"prt_15b077a6a001IBxTPWZTUP5REO","sessionID":"ses_ea4f89b40ffeJA5Vf8sjCWqpcq","messageID":"msg_15b0767350010wHqvIDshhxF9C"}}
