{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792529106453,"sessionID":"ses_ea4f89b40ffeJA5Vf8sjCWqpcq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_00_ET_Hwm94IolI5sobcrezQRw8733","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\src\\community\\geocache-milestone-card\\v1\\geocache-milestone-card.ts","newString":"  \"solution\": [\n    \"One card per count, from numbers typed in, never fetched. The props mirror the My Finds GPX fields: findCount, the cache-type mix, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, sinceYear. It draws the count as the hero, the type mix as a full-width bar, and three FTF / difficulty / terrain tiles.\",\n    \"The decision that matters: the milestone is computed, never typed. The card derives the ordinal (1,000th) and whether the count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the MILESTONE badge only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about.\"\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"command\": \"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @card.json -o card.png\",\n    \"try\": [\n      \"card.json: {\\\"cacherName\\\":\\\"GeoHiker\\\",\\\"findCount\\\":1042,\\\"typeMix\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Traditional\\\",\\\"count\\\":900}]}\",\n      \"findCount 1042 prints 1,042nd with no badge; 1500 and 2000 print it (Project-GC milestones)\",\n      \"-w 1920 -h 1080 puts the header beside the hero; -h 1920 stacks the bands\",\n      \"footer \\\"\\\" removes the sample line; accent \\\"#b3261e\\\" recolours the hero and badge\"\n    ]\n  },","oldString":"  \"solution\": [\n    \"One card per count, from numbers typed in, never fetched. The props mirror the My Finds GPX fields: findCount, the cache-type mix, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, sinceYear. It draws the count as the hero, the Project-GC milestone and the ordinal (1,000th) derived from it, the type mix as a full-width bar, and three FTF / difficulty / terrain tiles.\",\n    \"The decision that matters: the milestone is computed, never typed. The big number is the find count; the card derives the ordinal and whether that count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the MILESTONE badge only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about, so the card cannot disagree with itself.\"\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"command\": \"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @card.json -o card.png\",\n    \"try\": [\n      \"card.json: {\\\"cacherName\\\":\\\"GeoHiker\\\",\\\"findCount\\\":1042,\\\"typeMix\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Traditional\\\",\\\"count\\\":900}],\\\"ftfCount\\\":31,\\\"avgD\\\":2.1,\\\"avgT\\\":1.9}\",\n      \"findCount 1042 prints 1,042nd with no badge; 1500 and 2000 print the badge (Project-GC milestones)\",\n      \"-w 1920 -h 1080 puts the header beside the hero; -h 1920 stacks the four bands\",\n      \"footer \\\"\\\" removes the sample line; accent \\\"#b3261e\\\" recolours the hero number and badge\"\n    ]\n  },"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\src\\community\\geocache-milestone-card\\v1\\geocache-milestone-card.ts\n===================================================================\n--- C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\src\\community\\geocache-milestone-card\\v1\\geocache-milestone-card.ts\n+++ C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\src\\community\\geocache-milestone-card\\v1\\geocache-milestone-card.ts\n@@ -551,18 +551,18 @@\n   \"https://www.geocaching.com/help/index.php?id=118&pg=kb.page\",\n   \"https://www.yogosc.org/announcements/congratulations-to-geohiker55-on-1000-finds\"\n ],\n \"solution\": [\n-  \"One card per count, from numbers typed in, never fetched. The props mirror the My Finds GPX fields: findCount, the cache-type mix, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, sinceYear. It draws the count as the hero, the Project-GC milestone and the ordinal (1,000th) derived from it, the type mix as a full-width bar, and three FTF / difficulty / terrain tiles.\",\n-  \"The decision that matters: the milestone is computed, never typed. The big number is the find count; the card derives the ordinal and whether that count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the MILESTONE badge only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about, so the card cannot disagree with itself.\"\n+  \"One card per count, from numbers typed in, never fetched. The props mirror the My Finds GPX fields: findCount, the cache-type mix, ftfCount, avgD, avgT, sinceYear. It draws the count as the hero, the type mix as a full-width bar, and three FTF / difficulty / terrain tiles.\",\n+  \"The decision that matters: the milestone is computed, never typed. The card derives the ordinal (1,000th) and whether the count is a Project-GC milestone, and shows the MILESTONE badge only when it is. Nobody hand-writes the thing the whole post is about.\"\n ],\n \"usage\": {\n   \"command\": \"m0saic make @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 --props @card.json -o card.png\",\n   \"try\": [\n-    \"card.json: {\\\"cacherName\\\":\\\"GeoHiker\\\",\\\"findCount\\\":1042,\\\"typeMix\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Traditional\\\",\\\"count\\\":900}],\\\"ftfCount\\\":31,\\\"avgD\\\":2.1,\\\"avgT\\\":1.9}\",\n-    \"findCount 1042 prints 1,042nd with no badge; 1500 and 2000 print the badge (Project-GC milestones)\",\n-    \"-w 1920 -h 1080 puts the header beside the hero; -h 1920 stacks the four bands\",\n-    \"footer \\\"\\\" removes the sample line; accent \\\"#b3261e\\\" recolours the hero number and badge\"\n+    \"card.json: {\\\"cacherName\\\":\\\"GeoHiker\\\",\\\"findCount\\\":1042,\\\"typeMix\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"Traditional\\\",\\\"count\\\":900}]}\",\n+    \"findCount 1042 prints 1,042nd with no badge; 1500 and 2000 print it (Project-GC milestones)\",\n+    \"-w 1920 -h 1080 puts the header beside the hero; -h 1920 stacks the bands\",\n+    \"footer \\\"\\\" remove